From ffc06d2d3f660ff4de2a4ecef45bb1fcc9d3a947 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 20:26:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add a full audit trail: auth events, connection lifecycle,
 and a viewer page
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Extends AUDIT_REPORT.md's "no audit trail for auth/connection events"
finding (High) end to end:

- Every connect action (Meta, Shopify, Google Ads, TikTok — paste-token,
  agency-token, OAuth, and auto-provision paths) now logs a
  connection.connect event with the account and client it touched.
- New disconnectConnection() action + a "Disconnect" control per connected
  account in Settings — there was previously no way to cut a client's ad
  account/store connection off short of editing the database by hand.
  Disconnecting flips status to "disconnected", which every live-report
  and health-check function already treats as inactive.
- Client portal auth events are now logged: login success, failed
  password, lockout triggered, and logout, plus the admin-side login
  management actions (create/update/enable/disable/unlock/delete).
- New /dashboard/activity page (audit log had no display UI before this —
  it was write-only) shows the most recent 200 events with the client name,
  action, and a compact detail summary. Linked from the sidebar.
- Connected-accounts list in Settings now labels each connection by client
  name, not just its raw ad-account/store name — previously indistinguishable
  which client a given connection belonged to when an agency has several.

